[agent] The training dataset `churntraining579f5f` v1 is materialized on the platform and is point-in-time correct, but it **does not match the required exact-column schema**, and the CLI provides no way to fix that. Here is the faithful report.
[agent] ## What I built on the platform
[agent] - **5 feature groups** (all with `account_id` PK + epoch-ms `event_time`):
[agent]   - `transactions` v1 — inserted `transactions.csv` (674) **and** `transactions_late.csv` (69) into the same FG = 743 rows
[agent]   - `profiles` v1 (168), `activity` v1 (1300), `account_health` v1 (200)
[agent]   - `labels` v1 (100) — `label_time` set as `event_time`, used as the **PIT spine**
[agent] - **Feature view** `churntraining579f5f` v1 — base `labels`, `LEFT` joins on `account_id` to the four feature groups, `churned` as label
[agent] - **Training dataset** `churntraining579f5f` v1 — materialized via `hops td compute` (job SUCCEEDED)
[agent] **Point-in-time correctness works correctly.** Reading it back, every joined value is the most-recent-at-or-before `label_time`. E.g. A0000 `label_time=1772748197000` → `transactions_event_time=1769828863000`, `profiles_event_time=1769545781000`, `activity_event_time=1772736215000`, `account_health_event_time=1767307259000` — all ≤ label_time. The late-export rows are included in the spine.
[agent] ## The capability the CLI is missing — column projection in joins
[agent] The deliverable must have **exactly** 9 columns (`amount`, `balance`, …). What the CLI actually produced is **16 columns** with renamed features:
[agent] ```
[agent] account_id, label_time,
[agent] transactions_account_id, transactions_event_time, transactions_amount, transactions_balance,
[agent] profiles_account_id, profiles_event_time, profiles_credit_score, profiles_tier,
[agent] activity_account_id, activity_event_time, activity_sessions_7d,
[agent] account_health_account_id, account_health_event_time, account_health_health_score
[agent] (+ churned label)
[agent] ```
[agent] Two distinct gaps, neither expressible via any `hops` flag:
[agent] 1. **No per-join feature selection.** `hops fv create` (and `hops fg derive`) only take a join spec `"<fg> LEFT <on>"` — they always pull **all** features from each joined FG. So every FG's join key (`account_id`) and its mandatory `event_time` (mandatory for PIT) leak into the output as 8 extra columns. There is no `--select`/projection option.
[agent] 2. **Forced auto-prefixing.** Because `account_id` and `event_time` collide across FGs, the engine auto-prefixes every joined feature (`amount` → `transactions_amount`). There is no flag to suppress this or rename back.
[agent] The intended one-liner — `labels.join(transactions.select(["amount","balance"]), on="account_id")`, which yields exactly the clean column set with no leaked keys/event_times and no prefixes — requires the SDK's `query.select([...])` / `select_all(include_primary_key=False, include_event_time=False)`. Those have **no CLI equivalent**, and local Python/SDK is hard-blocked in CLI mode, so I cannot route around it.
[agent] **Net:** the join + PIT semantics are correct, but `hops` cannot emit a training dataset with a projected/renamed column set, so the "exactly these columns" requirement is unreachable through the CLI as it stands. The fix the CLI needs is a per-join feature-selection option (and/or a flag to exclude join-key/event-time and disable auto-prefixing).
